---
/**
 * Smoke test for the shell, not the real homepage.
 *
 * It exists so that phase 1 can prove the layout, the figures collection, the rung
 * mark and the callout all render together on a static page. The editorial pass
 * replaces every word of it.
 */
import Callout from "~/components/Callout.astro";
import Figure from "~/components/Figure.astro";
import Rung from "~/components/Rung.astro";
import Base from "~/layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Do the certain things first">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">Do the certain things first</h1>

    <p>
      Three parts of a portfolio pay you whatever the market does. Keep the fee low, put each
      holding in the account that taxes it least, and stop paying a fund manager to hand you a
      capital gain in December. That work is worth roughly 109 basis points a year against the
      portfolio a typical saver already holds, and you would know inside a year whether you got it.
    </p>

    <p>
      Everything after that is a wager. This site tells you which is which.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-10 grid gap-8 sm:grid-cols-3">
    <Figure id="structural-budget" />
    <Figure id="edge-vs-cheap-index" />
    <Figure id="effective-bets" />
  </div>

  <div class="prose mt-12">
    <h2>How sure we are, in four words</h2>

    <p>
      Every claim on this site carries one of four rungs. The mark beside the word is drawn in ink
      alone, at four intensities, so it survives a printout and a colour-blind reader. Nothing here
      is ever green for good news.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-6 flex flex-col gap-3">
    <Rung level="settled" showGloss />
    <Rung level="probably" showGloss />
    <Rung level="might" showGloss />
    <Rung level="cant-tell" showGloss />
  </div>

  <Callout kind="do-this">
    <p>
      Open your plan statement and read one number: the expense ratio on the fund holding most of
      your money. Under 10 basis points, skip to the next section. Over 50, you have found the
      largest reliable gain available to you today.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <div class="prose mt-12">
    <h2>Where the money actually comes from</h2>

    <p>
      The three benchmarks below answer different questions, and their results may never be added
      together. A saving measured against your own current holdings says nothing about whether you
      beat an index fund.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto">
    <table class="w-full max-w-measure border-collapse text-sm">
      <thead>
        <tr class="border-b border-rule-strong text-left">
          <th class="eyebrow py-2 pr-4">Compared with</th>
          <th class="eyebrow py-2 pr-4 text-right">Edge</th>
          <th class="eyebrow py-2 pr-4 text-right">Spread</th>
          <th class="eyebrow py-2">How sure</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody class="text-ink-muted">
        <tr class="border-b border-rule">
          <td class="py-2 pr-4">The portfolio you hold now</td>
          <td data-numeric class="py-2 pr-4 text-right">109 bp/yr</td>
          <td data-numeric class="py-2 pr-4 text-right">41 bp</td>
          <td class="py-2"><Rung level="settled" /></td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-rule">
          <td class="py-2 pr-4">A cheap total-market index</td>
          <td data-numeric class="py-2 pr-4 text-right">5.4 bp/yr</td>
          <td data-numeric class="py-2 pr-4 text-right">313 bp</td>
          <td class="py-2"><Rung level="cant-tell" /></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="py-2 pr-4">The average investor's behaviour</td>
          <td data-numeric class="py-2 pr-4 text-right">15 bp/yr</td>
          <td data-numeric class="py-2 pr-4 text-right">150 bp</td>
          <td class="py-2"><Rung level="might" /></td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <Callout kind="change-your-mind">
    <p>
      A fund shelf that cut its published edge below 20 basis points a year, or a decade of live
      returns in which the tilted sleeves trailed the index by more than their stated spread, would
      move the second row from a coin flip to a rejection.
    </p>
  </Callout>
</Base>
